le the percentages vary by period.","period_end":"2026-06-27"},{"type":"related_party_exposure","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report recurring, substantial purchases and payables with ATMP joint ventures in which AMD holds a 15% interest.","period_end":"2025-03-29"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report a $900 million favorable tax-provision impact after the March 2025 quarter from IRS approval.","period_end":"2025-03-29"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report the ZT Systems acquisition closing after the March 2025 quarter, followed by a $4.4 billion recorded purchase consideration.","period_end":"2025-03-29"},{"type":"subsequent_event","origin":"ai","summary":"The filings report a subsequent $2.4 billion cash receipt when AMD completed the sale of the ZT Manufacturing Business to Sanmina.","period_end":"2025-09-27"}],"narratives":[{"period_end":"2025-09-27","narrative":"The filing identified $139 million of remaining performance obligations expected to be recognized in the next 12 months [af4f49b6-290c-44e4-874b-c6e440070c10]. It also reported $413 million of contingent consideration liability [00e8f6d1-f0f1-4ecb-9372-a011894c6e1f] and a subsequent $2.4 billion cash receipt from the ZT Manufacturing Business sale [cb9c1a16-63ac-41c9-8c03-75016ae418b0]."},{"period_end":"2025-12-27","narrative":"No statement rewrite is supported by a dated quarter-sized currency claim in the catalog. The filing reported approximately $12.2 billion of unconditional commitments [0f5a7487-12f8-456f-94d4-5789d2c48cce] and a conditional contingent cash consideration of up to $450 million [b7881478-0e84-47d3-833f-213b3c9d0244]."},{"period_end":"2026-03-28","narrative":"The filing identified $167 million of remaining performance obligations expected to be recognized in the next 12 months [a6f0201c-c5e9-41ca-bc58-de909654f119]. It also reported maximum gross exposure of $4.1 billion from commercial-partner data-center lease guarantees [72f5ef81-3bfa-443d-84fc-191f3ed8459b]."},{"period_end":"2026-06-27","narrative":"The filing identified $144 million of remaining performance obligations expected to be recognized in the next 12 months [e6995728-2bb1-4a16-9eb2-f5dde98a933e]. It also reported $17,386 million of unconditional commitments for the remainder of fiscal 2026 [533fe4ba-459a-4ea3-a551-e8b3241e9aa1] and $4.5 billion of uncommenced lease payments [e99430b7-e32c-4dd9-8126-345be6638322]."}],"prose":{"overview":"Revenue grew 32% per year while expenses grew 31%, leaving a much larger operating scale than the $222 million backlog. The backlog is small beside $41.3 billion of trailing-year revenue.","debt":"Committed obligations total $4.3 billion, or 1.3x reported debt of $3.2 billion. Leases account for $1.1 billion of the committed total beyond debt.","wall":"The next 5 years carry $70.8 billion of obligations against $594 million of future revenue promised for that period. That is a 119.2x gap between amounts due and revenue promised.","flags_note":"The largest disclosed exposure is $4.1 billion tied to guarantees of commercial partners' data-center lease obligations. Other notable items include $1.3 billion to $4.5 billion tied to future data-center and real-estate lease payments that had not yet commenced, and an unsecured parent guarantee tied to ZT Systems' credit facility of approximately $642 million. The disclosures also describe an $800 million export-control inventory charge followed by a $360 million reversal in the same fiscal year's fourth quarter, plus recurring substantial purchases and payables tied to ATMP joint ventures in which AMD holds a 15% interest."}}